/-!
# KIL2: running a list of steps, interchanges delegated to child procedures

`runCode scode jOf steps` is item-language code (`IStmt`, so it may `call` procedures):
a shift step runs the code `scode s`, an interchange `swap a b` is the call `.call (jOf a b)`.

* `runCode_spec`: given IRuns specs of the shift codes and of the children (stack `0` holds the
  array, every other stack is restored), the code computes `runC Λ child 0 steps xs`, the
  `AModelProp11` denotation, with cost `Σ_steps (shift cost | child cost + 2) + 1`.
* `runCode_runArr`: with correct children this is `runArr Λ 0 steps xs`.
* `scode1`, `runCode1_spec`: the concrete instance where every shift has unit coefficient `1`
  (Lemma 10 case), implemented by `shP` (`KIL2Shift`); cost `cShift` per shift.
